// Myrnohrad, part III, The frost (Мороз): the night of 19-20 January 2026. About -15 °C and 3-7 cm of snow (c15 §3;
// ERA5 for the night: -12 to -15 °C, 5 cm, overcast, a north-westerly of 7-12 km/h); no moon (new on the 18th, its
// crescent set by evening: `sun::moon`). The town is half theirs, the front line north of the railway (ISW, 28 Dec);
// the garrison holds the northern quarters, the mine, Svitle and Rivne, fed by heavy drones and ground robots
// (c15 §2, 14-23 Jan). The night is not a battle: robots up the road and the Vampire over the roofs with fuel,
// food and rounds, the wounded out in the dark, their drones over the road at the night's tempo with the fibre ones
// failing in the ice (c15 §3), and single men seeping in from the jaw and the town's south. The dossier gives no
// numbers for the night; the rates and the times below are the design's, and say so. The schema is bav_core::data
// and bav_sim::data; the map is map.ron.
(
    date: "19 January 2026",
    tally_date: "19 JAN 2026",
    // 22:00 to about 04:00 in the day's 1500 s.
    day_start_min: 1320.0,
    compression: 0.24,
    season: Winter,
    // 19 January is the 19th day of the year; Kyiv on UTC+2. The moon is worked out for the date.
    sun: (19, 2.0),
    moon: (2026, 1, 19),
    overcast: true,
    wind: (0.25, 0.0, 2.8),
    // Most of the town's roofs gone by now; a few ruins smouldering in the snow; the cars of two months on the road.
    ruined: (0.6, 11),
    smouldering: 10,
    cars: [
        ((-1445.8, -213.4), 1.28),
        ((-2102.3, -382.4), 1.61),
        ((-517.5, -89.7), 2.04),
        ((721.8, -313.2), -1.4),
        ((-1577.9, -236.6), -1.4),
        ((428.1, -297.3), -1.31),
        ((-614.5, -94.7), -1.76),
        ((332.8, -285.0), -1.69),
        ((-1217.2, -152.5), -1.6),
        ((-1674.8, -263.9), 1.66),
        ((-750.0, -75.8), -1.46),
        ((-1721.7, -285.3), -1.35),
        ((-815.8, -94.3), 1.72),
        ((-449.5, -98.9), 1.12),
        ((168.1, -270.1), 2.22),
        ((-2084.5, -377.9), -1.38),
        ((74.7, -251.8), -1.71),
        ((201.0, -262.3), -1.0),
        ((-1923.3, -347.8), 1.04),
        ((-331.8, -138.5), 1.47),
        ((-1651.1, -252.7), -1.76),
        ((-1533.9, -233.4), -2.36),
        ((-341.5, -135.6), -1.08),
        ((-1187.5, -146.4), -1.68),
    ],
    words: (
        briefing: r#"MYRNOHRAD (МИРНОГРАД), THE ROAD INTO THE POCKET
THE NIGHT OF 19-20 JANUARY 2026

Minus fifteen, and a thin snow. Moscow claimed the town three weeks ago; the Russians are in about half of it,
south of the railway. The garrison holds the northern quarters, the Tsentralna mine, Svitle and Rivne, and
everything it eats and fires comes by night: on ground robots up the one road, and under heavy drones. Their FPVs
still hunt the road in the dark, on thermal; the cold freezes the fibre of both sides' drones. They no longer come
in threes: one man at a time, and now and then two.

You are the same drone team, moved north into the blocks by the mine, out of the basement that is now theirs.
The observers are up on the Tsentralna headframe. There is no moon tonight. The wounded wait for a robot.

The night will run whether or not you do anything. What you do matters at the margin.

Mouse: right-drag to look, wheel to zoom.  WASD: fly the drone.  Q/E: turn.  R/F: climb/descend.  I: thermal.
Left click: 155 mm fire mission (4 rounds).  4: an FPV.  C: drop a grenade from the drone.  J: our EW dome.
V: a ground robot for the wounded.  Alt+click: a robot with ammunition.  7: the robot's camera.
8: the Vampire with bombs (Shift+8 with a bundle); in it C drops, H brings it home.
1/2 or Tab: drone / the observers on the headframe.  M: move the drone team when they find you.  P: pause.  [ ]: time.

Press Enter."#,
        op_label: "OBSERVERS, THE TSENTRALNA HEADFRAME (СПОСТЕРІГАЧІ, КОПЕР ШАХТИ «ЦЕНТРАЛЬНА»)",
        op_lost: "The observers on the headframe are gone. No eyes from the mine.",
        forward_belt: "the ruins",
        mine_lines: ["Mine. He's stopped.", "Another one on a mine.", "Mine on the verge. That one's done."],
        closing: [
            "On 28 January their command posts and a commandant's office were in Myrnohrad. The marines in the north were told not to let them out. There was no order to leave.",
            "The same day ISW last saw Ukrainians in Pokrovsk.",
        ],
        keys: "R: the same night again, in the same frost.     Esc: quit.",
        sources: [
            (
                publisher: "Ukrainska Pravda",
                date: "28 Jan 2026",
                title: "Росіяни розгорнули в Мирнограді свою артилерію та штаби",
                url: "https://www.pravda.com.ua/news/2026/01/28/8018382/",
            ),
            (
                publisher: "Kyiv Independent",
                date: "Jan 2026",
                title: "Ukrainian infantry fight to survive on the Pokrovsk front as Russia closes in",
                url: "https://kyivindependent.com/if-you-stop-you-die-inside-ukraines-last-fight-for-pokrovsk-and-myrnohrad/",
            ),
            (
                publisher: "United24 Media",
                date: "Jan 2026",
                title: "Winter Is No Longer Russia's Ally on the Battlefield Near Pokrovsk",
                url: "https://united24media.com/latest-news/winter-is-no-longer-russias-ally-on-the-battlefield-near-pokrovsk-15284",
            ),
            (
                publisher: "Interfax-Ukraine",
                date: "14 Jan 2026",
                title: "Skhid force: Occupiers intensify attempts to infiltrate northern Pokrovsk; Defense Forces repelling them",
                url: "https://en.interfax.com.ua/news/general/1136424.html",
            ),
            (
                publisher: "Euromaidan Press",
                date: "2 Jan 2026",
                title: "Russia switches to one-by-one infiltrations near Pokrovsk, hoping to slip past unnoticed",
                url: "https://euromaidanpress.com/2026/01/02/russia-switches-to-one-by-one-infiltrations-near-pokrovsk-hoping-to-slip-past-unnoticed/",
            ),
            (
                publisher: "Euromaidan Press",
                date: "13 Jan 2026",
                title: "Ukraine's jam-proof drones have one weakness: icy weather",
                url: "https://euromaidanpress.com/2026/01/13/ukraines-jam-proof-drones-have-one-weakness-icy-weather/",
            ),
            (
                publisher: "Institute for the Study of War",
                date: "28 Dec 2025",
                title: "Russian Offensive Campaign Assessment, December 28, 2025",
                url: "https://understandingwar.org/research/russia-ukraine/russian-offensive-campaign-assessment-december-28-2025/",
            ),
        ],
    ),
    // The debrief's rows (the schema is the game's screen.rs); the tally's and the fire panel's lines are map.ron's.
    debrief: (
        rows: [
            Line("Their men sent in", Sent),
            Line("    dead", AttackerDead),
            Line("    came back", Returned),
            Line("Our casualties", DefenderLosses),
            Areas("{area} at dawn"),
            Line("Shells left", Shells),
            If(Drops, [Line("Grenades dropped from the drone", Drops)]),
            If(
                Robots,
                [
                    Line("Ground robots", Robots),
                    Line("    loads delivered", Delivered),
                    Line("Wounded brought out by robot", WoundedCarried),
                    Line("    still waiting", WoundedWaiting),
                ],
            ),
            If(Bomber, [Line("The Vampire's sorties", Sorties)]),
            If(
                Seep,
                [
                    Line("Their burrows in the northern quarters", Burrows),
                    Line("    found", BurrowsFound),
                    Line("    emptied", BurrowsEmptied),
                    Line("Their fire on our drone crew told", CrewsHit),
                ],
            ),
            If(Killzone, [Line("Their FPVs over the road", TheirSorties), Line("    what they hit", TheirHits)]),
        ],
    ),
    // The observers up the Tsentralna headframe, under its sheaves.
    op: ((1475.0, -248.0), 40.0),
    // The drone team in the five-storey blocks north of the mine's street, out of the western quarters' basement, which
    // is theirs by now (the block is the design's).
    team: (900.0, -700.0),

    // The pocket on 19 January: the town half theirs, the front line north of the railway (c15 §2, ISW 28 Dec), the
    // jaw closer over the north-east; the northern quarters, the mine, the villages and the road ours.
    pocket: (
        grey: [
            [
                (-5000.0, -380.0),
                (-2400.0, -360.0),
                (-1500.0, -80.0),
                (-300.0, 0.0),
                (400.0, -120.0),
                (1200.0, -150.0),
                (5000.0, -250.0),
                (5000.0, 5000.0),
                (-5000.0, 5000.0),
            ],
            [(200.0, -5000.0), (5000.0, -5000.0), (5000.0, -300.0), (1700.0, -420.0), (700.0, -1000.0)],
        ],
        theirs: [
            [
                (-5000.0, -200.0),
                (-2200.0, -150.0),
                (-1400.0, 250.0),
                (-300.0, 300.0),
                (400.0, 150.0),
                (1200.0, 100.0),
                (5000.0, 0.0),
                (5000.0, 5000.0),
                (-5000.0, 5000.0),
            ],
            [(700.0, -5000.0), (5000.0, -5000.0), (5000.0, -450.0), (1900.0, -650.0), (1100.0, -1200.0)],
        ],
    ),
    // The garrison's posts (c15 §2, 14-23 Jan: the north of the town, Svitle and Rivne held): Svitle, Rivne, the
    // town's western entrance north of the H-32, the blocks north of Tsentralna street, the northern quarters' south
    // edge over the drone team, the mine, and the northern quarters' east towards the jaw.
    ua_positions: [
        (-560.0, -1250.0),
        (-1750.0, -700.0),
        (-300.0, -350.0),
        (300.0, -450.0),
        (850.0, -520.0),
        (1400.0, -300.0),
        (1150.0, -650.0),
    ],

    // ---- The battle's part (bav_sim::data) ----
    // The night's robots (c15 §2, 14-23 Jan: the northern quarters supplied by heavy drones and UGVs; c15 §5: the
    // UGVs "usually don't survive the trip", the bombers lift 60 mm bombs and never 120 mm, keeping the drone teams in
    // fuel took many sorties): five ground robots and the Vampire's four sorties (the allotment's, below; the numbers
    // are the design's), and the wounded waiting for them: four of the robots the night's runs, the fifth for a call
    // that has waited an hour of the clock (`fetch`). Their FPVs over the road are the kill zone's below.
    robots: (casevac: true, fetch: 1.0, bomber: (endurance: 1000.0)),
    // What each post has to fire before it is dry, a robot's or a bundle's ammunition filling it by half: part I's
    // figure, the design's (the dossier gives none); the night asks whether the posts are fed (c15 §2, 14-23 Jan).
    post_ammo: 60,
    // The Record: riflemen at the seven posts, a battery's sixteen rounds, four FPVs, six grenades.
    allotment: (
        points: 80,
        supply: (4, 0.5),
        record: [
            (id: "rifles", at: 0),
            (id: "rifles", at: 1),
            (id: "rifles", at: 2),
            (id: "rifles", at: 3),
            (id: "rifles", at: 4),
            (id: "rifles", at: 5),
            (id: "rifles", at: 6),
            (id: "155", count: 1),
            (id: "fpv", count: 4),
            (id: "vog", count: 3),
            (id: "robot", count: 5),
            (id: "vampire", count: 4),
        ],
    ),
    // Their drones over the road at night (bav_sim::killzone; c15 §4, §5: thermal cameras made the night only a
    // little safer than the day), at about a third of part I's rates, a night's and the design's (c15 §11). The town's
    // south is theirs now, so Sudny Den flies from inside it; Rubikon is on the road all night; the Archangels' fibre
    // ones, and a waiter of theirs on the H-32's shoulder. Icing stops the spools and snaps the cable, and the fibre's
    // modules lose 20-50% in the cold (06, icing; Euromaidan Press, 13 Jan): a third of the fibre sorties snag, the
    // design's reading of it. The dome over the drone team, and nets over the H-32 from the road head to the town
    // (Kyiv Independent's photographs of January, c15 §11; no length is published, so the stretch is the design's),
    // and over the robots' track from the road head down to Rivne.
    // No car runs: nothing on wheels gets through (c15 §5).
    killzone: (
        crews: [
            (name: ("Rubikon", "Рубікон"), kind: Fibre, at: (600.0, 2900.0), per_hour: 4.0),
            (
                name: ("Sudny Den", "Судний день"),
                kind: Rf,
                at: (-200.0, 1400.0),
                per_hour: 3.0,
                relay: (300.0, 600.0),
            ),
            (
                name: ("the Irish", "«Ірландці»"),
                kind: Rf,
                at: (2800.0, -2300.0),
                per_hour: 2.0,
                relay: (2250.0, -1650.0),
            ),
            (name: ("the Archangels", "«Архангели»"), kind: Fibre, at: (2700.0, 2200.0), per_hour: 2.0),
            (name: ("the Archangels", "«Архангели»"), kind: Waiter, at: (-1240.0, -162.0), per_hour: 1.0),
        ],
        // The H-32 from the road head to the town's western entrance, "the single road into Myrnohrad" (c15 §5); in the
        // town the blocks and the ruins hide the street.
        watch: [
            [
                (-2304.0, -448.5),
                (-1795.4, -302.3),
                (-1573.0, -240.2),
                (-1240.7, -150.3),
                (-779.5, -83.9),
                (-415.7, -105.0),
                (-199.3, -202.5),
            ],
        ],
        domes: [(post: 4, radius: 300.0)],
        nets: [
            [
                (-2304.0, -448.5),
                (-1795.4, -302.3),
                (-1573.0, -240.2),
                (-1240.7, -150.3),
                (-779.5, -83.9),
                (-718.8, -82.4),
                (-415.7, -105.0),
            ],
            [
                (-2128.0, -398.0),
                (-2111.0, -393.0),
                (-2100.0, -415.0),
                (-2061.0, -504.0),
                (-2013.0, -607.0),
                (-1911.0, -567.0),
                (-1845.0, -593.0),
                (-1787.0, -633.0),
                (-1761.0, -676.0),
            ],
        ],
        team: 1.0,
        snag: 0.33,
    ),
    // The night (22:00 + 0.24 min a game second): robots and the Vampire through it, the wounded out as the robots
    // reach their posts, and single men seeping into the town's north, now and then two (c15 §5: single men by
    // January, Euromaidan Press 2 Jan; Interfax 14 Jan: attempts to infiltrate the north intensify), from the jaw
    // past the mine for the drone team, and out of the town's south for it too. About ten a day came in in
    // clear weather (c15 §5); the night's rate, about seven in six hours, is the design's, in the cold that killed
    // theirs too (c15 §3, the 7th Corps).
    script: [
        (2.0, Say("Bird up, thermal. Minus fifteen. The battery won't last long in this.")),
        (
            40.0,
            Say("All, this is {command}. Robots up the road tonight, and the Vampire. Keep the road clear for them."),
        ),
        // The robots go out early: at 10 km/h the northern quarters are three and a half kilometres and most of the
        // night from the road head. Fuel and batteries for the drone team, ammunition for the town's western entrance,
        // food for Rivne, ammunition for Svitle; each brings back the wounded waiting where it unloads.
        (5.0, Ugv(to: 4, cargo: Power)),
        (25.0, Ugv(to: 2, cargo: Ammo)),
        (60.0, Ugv(to: 1, cargo: Food)),
        (450.0, Ugv(to: 0, cargo: Ammo)),
        // The Vampire: rounds for the east post, bombs on the jaw's path, food for the mine, bombs on the town's south.
        (200.0, Sortie(to: (1150.0, -650.0), load: Bundle(Ammo))),
        (520.0, Sortie(to: (1750.0, -850.0), load: Bombs)),
        (880.0, Sortie(to: (1400.0, -300.0), load: Bundle(Food))),
        (1240.0, Sortie(to: (900.0, 250.0), load: Bombs)),
        (
            60.0,
            Seep(
                route: 1,
                from: 900.0,
                width: 250.0,
                per_hour: 0.6,
                crews: 1.0,
                men: (1, 2),
                label: "22:15  One at a time, from the jaw",
            ),
        ),
        (
            150.0,
            Seep(
                route: 0,
                from: 1150.0,
                width: 250.0,
                per_hour: 0.6,
                crews: 1.0,
                men: (1, 2),
                label: "22:35  Out of the town's south, for the drone team",
            ),
        ),
        (
            1000.0,
            Say("All, this is {command}. The cold is killing theirs too. Frostbite, hypothermia. They keep coming."),
        ),
        (1300.0, Say("This is {op}. Quiet now. Hours yet to first light.")),
    ],
)
